The files in this directory (data/receptors/) are group post-mortem receptor-density data from other people, not the
scanned person's:

- zilles2017_all_layers.csv: Zilles K, Palomero-Gallagher N (2017) Multiple transmitter receptors in regions and layers
  of the human cerebral cortex. Frontiers in Neuroanatomy 11:78, doi:10.3389/fnana.2017.00078, (c) 2017 Zilles and
  Palomero-Gallagher, Creative Commons Attribution License (CC BY). Supplementary Table 2, extracted unchanged, plus our
  approximate MNI centroid per area. Table mirrored from https://github.com/AlGoulas/receptor_principles (MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2020 AlGoulas).
- receptors_214.csv: an adaptation of the above: 7 receptors mapped onto the 200 Schaefer parcels by inverse-distance
  weighting (pipeline/build_receptors.py); subcortical rows left blank. Parcel centroids (c) 2016 Computational Brain
  Imaging Group (CBIG), MIT License, https://github.com/ThomasYeoLab/CBIG.

RECEPTORS_SOURCES.md records the sources that were looked at and not used (non-commercial or unclear licences).
